# FIXTURE SOURCE for bead inc-b4l3g.2 (tools/check_feed_upon_pain.sh): an orc
# priest of Khasrach with the Pain domain (Feed upon Pain, ability level 1),
# EMPTY weapon hand (so AttackMode() brawls: Punch 1d3+3), wounded to about 30/36
# hit points, carrying a Feed upon Pain tally of 6. Build it with
#
#   INCURSION_LOF_FORCE_ROLL=20 INCURSION_FORCE_DAMAGE_ROLL=3 \
#   tools/make_char_fixture.sh orc-priest-pain-seed1-sneakopts \
#       tools/keys/pain-priest-wounded-save.keys 1 tools/fixtures/options-sneak-invis.dat
#
# The two INCURSION_* variables are part of the recipe (the fixture sheet cannot
# record them): they make a summoned giant rat bite for a known 2 and make the
# priest's one punch deal a known 6, which is the carried tally.
#
# WHY WOUNDED. Feed upon Pain heals only up to max HP, so a full-HP priest reads
# healed=0 on every blow and the heal cannot be asserted. Seed 1 deals this kit
# with both hands empty, so no weapon swap is needed.
# WHY A TALLY OF 6. The first blow then always crosses a 10 (6+4 at least; a
# fatigued, unsurprised blow deals 4), so the check sees a heal whatever the
# target's hit points.
# The rat bites while the priest rests; resting is cut short while a hostile is
# in view, so many rests are sent. Then the priest punches the rat once, kills
# every monster, and searches until the status bar reads Exploring (a loaded
# game still in Fighting makes tools/keys/load-char-sheet.keys' search eat a key).

a
n
y
@choose "Orc"
@choose "Orc (Standard)"
@choose "Priest"
@choose "Khasrach"
a
@choose "Chaotic Evil"
a
d
a
a
a a
@while "|  *" RIGHT RIGHT RIGHT DOWN
ENTER y
y
a
@expect "Learn Spells: Level"    # the starting-spells checklist
SPACE DOWN SPACE DOWN SPACE DOWN SPACE DOWN    # mark the first rows; a full level refuses the rest
SPACE DOWN SPACE DOWN SPACE DOWN SPACE DOWN
ENTER

SPACE
@dump:played

w
y
ESC

w
@choose "Monster Summoning"
@choose "Animals"
@choose "giant rat"
RIGHT ENTER
@until "HP:" ESC
. . . . . . . . . .
. . . . . . . . . .
. . . . .
@dump:wounded
RIGHT
@while "Die?" n
@dump:punched

w
@choose "Genocide Everything"
@dump:cleared
s
@dump:calm

@until "System Menu" ESC
@expect "System Menu"
b
@dump:saved
